    narr:narration """On 20260719, CTO Quinton Fairweather issued what the graph records as a formal adoption decision: [Zypherion adoption declared](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_1), grounded in a [15x columnar-query performance claim](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_2) and locked to a [next-quarter migration start](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_3). An editorial layer (XenaExpertgh, same date) restates the same three beats as summary bullets: [database selection](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_4), [performance figure](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_5), and [Q3 2026 timeline](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1LifecycleStepA_6). The graph is narrow and internally consistent at this snapshot — a single decision moment, two voices, no subsequent revision visible here. What is not present: rationale beyond the performance number, alternatives considered, dissent, or any post-decision update.""" ;
